<title>UK: HORSE RACING-RESULTS OF FEATURE RACES AT EPSOM.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-RESULTS OF FEATURE RACES AT EPSOM.</headline>
<dateline>EPSOM, England 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of feature races</p>
<p>at Epsom on Friday:</p>
<p>Coronation Cup, group one race for four-year-olds and</p>
<p>upwards, run over one mile and four furlongs (2.4 kms):</p>
<p>1. Singspiel  5-4 favourite (ridden by Frankie Dettori)</p>
<p>2. Dushyantor 9-2 (Kieren Fallon)</p>
<p>3. Le Destin 14-1 (Thierry Gillet)</p>
<p>Five ran:</p>
<p>Distances: Five lengths, half a length.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Sheikh Mohammed, trained in England by</p>
<p>Michael Stoute.</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: 113,895 pounds sterling ($184,965).</p>
<p>Epsom Oaks (for three-year-old fillies, run over 12 furlongs</p>
<p>(2.4 km)</p>
<p>1. Reams of Verse 5-6 favourite (Kieren Fallon)</p>
<p>2. Gazelle Royale 33-1 (Jimmy Fortune)</p>
<p>3. Crown of Light 11-1 (Olivier Peslier)</p>
<p>Twelve ran:</p>
<p>Distances: One and a half lengths, three quarters of a</p>
<p>length.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Prince Khalid Abdullah and trained in</p>
<p>England by Henry Cecil. Value to winner $310,000</p>
</text>
